<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>9.3.6: Lesson Summary</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m02377</md:content-id>
    <md:title>9.3.6: Lesson Summary</md:title>
    <md:uuid>a263dbb2-c2a3-4d3e-aa02-78af2e4b0f7d</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
  <section><para>In this lesson, you learned how to:</para>
<list>
  <item> Solve by completing the square when given a quadratic equation in which the coefficient of the squared term is 1.</item>
</list>
<para>Here are th <emphasis>ctivities</emphasis> that helped you reach those goals:</para>
<list>
  <item> 9.3.1: Solving Equations with Fractions</item>
  <list>
    <item> In this activity, you mentally solved equations with fractions and exponents.</item>
  </list>
  <item> 9.3.2: Using Completing the Square to Solve Equations</item>
  <list>
    <item> In this activity, you solved quadratic equations involving rational numbers including decimals and fractions.</item>
    <item> 9.3.2: Self Check</item>
    <item> 9.3.2: Additional Resources</item>
  </list>
  <item> 9.3.3: Solve by Completing the Square</item>
  <list>
    <item> In this activity, you examined the steps to solving quadratic equations by completing the square and identified the step where an error occurred.</item>
    <item> 9.3.3: Self Check</item>
    <item> 9.3.3: Additional Resources</item>
  </list>
  <item> 9.3.4: Completing the Square with Fractions</item>
  <list>
    <item> In this activity, you showed how to get the given zeros of the quadratic by completing the square.</item>
  </list>
</list>
<para>After these activities, you completed the following <emphasis>practice</emphasis>:</para>
<list>
  <item> 9.3.5: Practice</item>
</list>
<section class="checking-in"><title>Checking In</title><exercise id="_29b3aac8-c795-45dc-9226-667245e97861" class="multiple-choice"><problem><para>On a scale of 1 to 5, how confident do you feel about the learning goals of this lesson?</para></problem><solution><para>Correct!</para><para>Nice reflection! You learn more when you take the time to reflect on your thinking.</para></solution></exercise></section></section>
</content>
</document>
